Subject: [PATCH] cacheinfo: complete architecture fallback for the first CPU

The SK-D840N DT has no cache nodes. Linux 6.12.103 sets use_arch_info when
architecture-derived cache information is available, but returns the old
DT/ACPI error. The first CPU therefore fails cache_shared_cpu_map_setup(),
while subsequent CPUs skip cache_setup_properties(). Clear the error only
when the existing architecture fallback has been selected.

This target-local fix does not invent cache sizes, add hardware cache
controls, or suppress errors on architectures without the fallback.

Source: gregkh/linux v6.12.103 drivers/base/cacheinfo.c
Source-blob: 89410127089b934a4a6871c88cd1aef67846588d
Related discussion: https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/06/11/980

---
--- a/drivers/base/cacheinfo.c
+++ b/drivers/base/cacheinfo.c
@@ -333,8 +333,10 @@
 		ret = cache_setup_acpi(cpu);
 
 	// Assume there is no cache information available in DT/ACPI from now.
-	if (ret && use_arch_cache_info())
+	if (ret && use_arch_cache_info()) {
 		use_arch_info = true;
+		ret = 0;
+	}
 
 	return ret;
 }
